Description: Lex Twig 3.17 number literals with "_" and exponents
 Twig 3.17 accepts digit separators ("1_000", "1_000.500_1") and exponents
 with an optional sign ("1e3", "1.5e-3", "2.5E+10"). twig-lexer 1.0.0 uses
 Twig 2's "[0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)?", so "1_000" became NUMBER "1" plus NAME
 "_000" and "1e3" became NUMBER "1" plus NAME "e3". numberPattern is now a
 JavaScript form of Twig's REGEX_NUMBER (LNUM, FRAC and EXPONENT). Token
 values stay as written in the source, so the lexer remains lossless.
 Twig 3.0 to 3.16 required a sign in the exponent; 3.17 made it optional.
Author: Numiko
Origin: other, https://github.com/twigphp/Twig/blob/v3.17.0/src/Lexer.php
Forwarded: not-needed
Twig-Reference: 3.17.0 ("Support underscores in number literals")
Test: test/fixtures/twig/numbers.twig (parity with Twig 3.28.0); npm run test:upstream
Last-Update: 2026-11-03
---
diff --git a/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts b/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts
index 444b28c..81114d8 100644
--- a/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts
+++ b/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ export const namePattern: string = '[a-zA-Z_\\x7f-\\uffff][a-zA-Z0-9_\\x7f-\\uff
 /**
  * The regular expression pattern used to identify a number.
  */
-export const numberPattern: string = '[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]+)?';
+export const numberPattern: string = '[0-9]+(?:_[0-9]+)*(?:\\.[0-9]+(?:_[0-9]+)*)?(?:[eE][+-]?[0-9]+(?:_[0-9]+)*)?';
 
 /**
